.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL = Element>
.br
class csmp::PT_op< dim, CELL >"\fBPoint\fP sources, loads etc\&. for vector solution variable\&. In mechanics, this operator is known as nodal force vector\&. 


.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
S\&.K\&. Matthai 

.PP
S\&. Roberts 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
2000
.RE
.PP
Use this operand to accumulate nodal vector-type properties flagged Dirichlet into the righthand side of the global matrix equation\&.

.PP
The forces are distributed onto the Dirichlet nodes such that nodes which are shared by two elements are accumulated correctly:

.PP
F(midpoint node) = (F / boundary-nodes) F(corner node) = (F / boundary-nodes) / 2 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL = Element> \fBPT_op\fP< dim, CELL > * \fBcsmp::PT_op\fP< dim, CELL >::clone () const\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Implements \fBcsmp::MathOperatorRHS< dim, Element >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL> void \fBcsmp::PT_op\fP< dim, CELL >::ComputeContribution (const CELL< dim > & e)\fR [final]\fP, \fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"
Accumulates nodal vector forces from nodes which are flagged Dirichlet with regard to the target variable\&. The \fBOperand\fP is therefore a node variable\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The element from which accumulation into the global matrix takes place and the time-increment over which the force will be applied\&. 
.br

.PP
The result gets stored into the MathOperator right-hand vector\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To compute nodal forces acting on the boundary of a model\&. 
.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::MathOperatorRHS< dim, Element >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL> void \fBcsmp::PT_op\fP< dim, CELL >::GetOperands (const CELL< dim > & e)\fR [final]\fP, \fR [override]\fP"
Reads node data (=vector properties) for further processing by the \fBComputeContribution()\fP method\&. 

